//! The `mask-image` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the image
//! that is used as the mask layer for an element, hiding sections of the element on which the
//! masking image is set based on the alpha channel of the mask image and, depending on the
//! `mask-mode` property value, the luminance of the mask image's colors.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - none: This keyword is interpreted as a transparent black image layer.
//!
//! Grammar: <mask-reference>#
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-masking-1/#propdef-mask-image
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/mask-image
